  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1212 PM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nA cold front will continue to move through the area this afternoon \nand reach our eastern zones by this evening. Winds ahead of this \nfront will be from the southwest with winds behind this front form \nthe north at an increase in speed. A few strong to severe storms \nmay form along and ahead this boundary late afternoon into this \nevening generally east of Hays to Dodge to Liberal with the best \nchance across south central Kansas. Any storms that do form should \nmove out of the area by midnight with decreasing cloudiness from west \nto east. Strong northerly winds will be felt behind this front this \nevening gusting to over 30 mph at times. High pressure will then \nsettle into the area tomorrow with continued northerly winds. Winds \nthen become light and variable tomorrow afternoon into tomorrow \nevening. Winds then shift to the southeast tomorrow night into \nMonday as lee troughing develops across eastern Colorado. Skies will \nbe mostly clear tomorrow with some high level cloudiness tomorrow \nnight into Monday. As for temperatures, Highs this afternoon will \nreach into the 60s across south central Kansas with 50s elsewhere \ndue to the cold front. Cold air advection filters into the area \ntonight with lows ranging from the upper 20s across west central \nKansas to mid 30s across south central Kansas. Highs tomorrow only \nlook to reach into the 40s with lows tomorrow night in the 20s. Wind \nchills in the upper teens will be possible across all areas Monday \nmorning besides south central Kansas. Highs Monday will once again \nonly reach into the 40s. \n\nIn the Extended, a weak disturbance will move out of the Rockies \nMonday night into Tuesday morning bringing a slight chance of \nprecipitation across far western Kansas. Temperatures may be cold \nenough for some snow to fall but little to no accumulation is \nanticipated at this time. Dry conditions are then expected through \nthe remainder of the forecast as upper level ridging moves over the \nPlains. Temperatures during this time frame will be in the 40s \nTuesday through Thursday with 50s Friday into this weekend. Lows \nwill be in the 20s with low 30s returning this weekend.",
